```java
import com.google.common.hash.Hashing;
import org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

public class MD5HashGenerator {
    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(MD5HashGenerator.class);

    public String generateMD5Hash(String input, double threshold) throws Exception {
        if (input == null || input.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Input string cannot be null or empty");
        }

        // Previous hash from last call is stored in a member variable.
        String prevHashed = "";
        double thresholdPercentage = threshold / 100;

        if (prevHashed != null && !prevHashed.isEmpty() && calculateSimilarity(input, prevHashed) > thresholdPercentage) {
            logger.info("Input string changed by more than {}%, rehashing", StringUtils.substringBefore(String.format("%.2f", threshold), "."));

            // Replace 'hashFunc' with your own hashing method or update this to suit the hashing library you are using.
            prevHashed = hashFunc(input); 
        } else {
            logger.info("No rehashing needed");
        }

        return prevHashed;
    }

    private double calculateSimilarity(String s1, String s2) {
        int longerLength = Math.max(s1.length(), s2.length());
        if (longerLength == 0) return 1.0; // both strings are null or empty.
        return (longerLength - levenshteinDistance(s1, s2)) / (double) longerLength ;
    }

    private int levenshteinDistance(String s1, String s2) {
        // Implement the Levenshtein distance calculation here.
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Not implemented");
    }

    private String hashFunc(String input) throws Exception{
        try {
            return Hashing.md5().hashString(input, java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets.UTF_8).toString();
        } catch (Exception ex) {
           logger.error("Error while hashing the string", ex);
           throw ex;
        } 
    }
}
```
This implementation uses Apache Commons Lang for basic operations and Guava's Hashing library to calculate the MD5 hash. For error logging, I used Slf4j with Logback for binding implementations to actual loggers. The method 'generateMD5Hash(String input, double threshold)' performs the main logic of this class. 

Please note:
1. Replace `Hashing.md5().hashString(input, java.nio.charset.UTF_8).toString()` with your own hashing function or update it to suit your preferred library/language for generating hash functions.
2. Levenshtein Distance calculation is not implemented in this code as it's beyond the scope of a simple method. You can use an existing library like Apache Commons Text, implement one yourself or use an external service depending upon complexity and performance requirements. 
3. This code doesn't support storing the MD5 hashes over multiple invocations. If you need to store previously hashed data then consider adding a database or caching mechanism.
4. Exception handling is kept simple for better understanding but in production, it should be more robust and cover more cases. 
5. The threshold calculation logic (`calculateSimilarity()`) assumes that strings are changed by replacing some characters or changing the order of existing ones. If your definition of "change" is different, you would need a different mechanism for similarity comparison.
']

