The cleanup function securely deallocates the cipher context and resets all sensitive data to prevent memory leaks. This is done by calling `OPENSSL_cleanse()`, which overwrites the given buffer with zeroes before releasing it, which makes it more difficult for an attacker to gain information about its contents.
