['Here's an example to illustrate how you might write a multi-threaded Java class with above requirements. For brevity and simplicity reasons I will only provide the core classes that handle MD5 hashing and thread safety. The rest of your requirements will require additional code to implement fully:

```java
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue;
import java.util.concurrent.LinkedBlockingDeque;
import javax.xml.bind.DatatypeConverter;

public class MD5HashWorker {
    private static final int MAX_CAPACITY = 1024 * 1024 * 50; // 50 MB

    private BlockingQueue<String> queue = new LinkedBlockingDeque<>(MAX_CAPACITY);
    private volatile boolean shutdownRequested = false;

    public void start() {
        Thread thread = new Thread(() -> {
            while (!shutdownRequested) {
                try {
                    String item = queue.take(); // blocks if the queue is empty
                    System.out.println("Processing: " + item);

                    String hash = computeMD5Hash(item);
                    // process hashed string...
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                }
            }
        });

        thread.start();
    }

    public void stop() {
        shutdownRequested = true;
        // this will wake up the consumer if it's sleeping because of queue being empty
        queue.notifyAll(); 
    }

    public boolean enqueue(String item) {
        return queue.offer(item);
    }

    private String computeMD5Hash(String input) {
        try {
            MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");
            md.update(input.getBytes());
            byte[] digest = md.digest();
            return DatatypeConverter.printHexBinary(digest).toLowerCase();
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new AssertionError("MD5 algorithm not available.", e); // can't happen
        }
    }
}
```
Please note, this is a simplified example that only provides the core functionality of processing strings and calculating their MD5 hashes. The rest of your requirements involve additional complexity to handle (like configuration management, logging, dynamic resizing, monitoring, periodic rehashing and expiration). Additionally, this code lacks proper error handling and doesn't include any form of resource cleanup which would be necessary for a production system.
