ListNode* head = NULL;
pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

void add(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T value) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    ListNode* newNode = malloc(sizeof(ListNode));
    if(newNode == NULL) exit(-1); // Handle error case properly.

    newNode->data = value;
    newNode->next = head;
    head = newNode;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}

void clearList() {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    while(head != NULL) {
        ListNode* nextNode = head->next;
        free(head);
        head = nextNode;
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}
```
This code uses a singly linked list to manage the structures. To ensure thread safety, we use a mutex which only allows one thread to modify the list at a time. When adding a new value, we allocate memory for a new node and add it to the front of the list. The `clearList` function frees all nodes in the list by traversing through them and freeing each one after saving its 'next' pointer.

