readFilesInDir('/path/to/directory', /\.txt$/, emitter);
```
This script will recursively read all text files in a directory and emit an event with the file's content when it is done reading, logging any errors that occur during the process. This script uses async to limit concurrency to 10 at a time using a queue, which prevents system overload due to too many file reads at once. It also includes basic error handling: if a file read fails, it will be retried after a delay.
